<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Brazil's Telerj raised.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Brazil's Telerj raised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>HSBC James Capel analyst Paul Aran raised his rating for Brazilian telephone company Telerj Thursday to buy from long-term buy.</p>
<p>-- &quot;We estimate Telerj's asset value at $9.1 billion net of debt, or about $310 per share,&quot; he wrote in a report.</p>
<p>-- &quot;Our 18-month price target of 269 reais assumes the shares are fairly valued at a 20-percent discount to asset value.&quot;</p>
<p>-- The company's preferred shares were down 1.90 reais to 153.10 reais in Sao Paulo. Telerj is a unit of federal telephone holding Telebras SA.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
